  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.0: One failure stage enumeration per operation — RecycleFailureStage is gone, replaced by ListFailureStage, EmptyFailureStage, RecyclePathFailureStage and RestoreFailureStage, and RecycleFailure is now RecycleFailure<TStage>, so a stage an operation cannot produce will not compile against it. An entry an empty could not remove reports EmptyFailureStage.EntryNotRemoved rather than sharing Enumeration with a walk that failed. Breaking: the stage values are renumbered, so an int persisted against RecycleFailureStage no longer names a member\n            1.2.0: Progress reporting on RecycleAsync, RestoreAsync and EmptyAsync — each settings type carries OnItemProcessed, OnProgressFailed and WaitForProgressCallbacks, and each handler is given a RecycleProgress, a RestoreProgress or an EmptyProgress. EmptyAsync gains an overload taking EmptyOptions\n            1.1.0: Support for the first version of the Recycle Bin index file, on machines whose Windows reads that one rather than the second\n            1.0.0: First release",
